  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p>New Delhi: The <a href=\"/tag/national+pharmaceutical+pricing+authority\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">National Pharmaceutical Pricing Authority</a> has extended the validity of the existing ceiling prices for <a href=\"/tag/orthopaedic+knee+implants\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">orthopaedic knee implants</a> used in knee replacement systems by two months, until January 15, 2027.As per a notification in the Press Gazette, the extension comes as the authority considers representations received from manufacturers and industry associations.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The existing price controls were last extended on November 14, 2025, and were due to remain in force until November 15, 2026.The move comes amid growing demands for <a href=\"/tag/trade+margin+rationalisation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">trade margin rationalisation</a> for medical devices.The <a href=\"/tag/association+of+indian+medical+device+industry\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Association of Indian Medical Device Industry</a> (AiMed), Forum Director, Rajiv Nath said, \"AiMeD welcomes and is highly appreciative of NPPA's decision to extend the existing ceiling prices of knee implants while stakeholder representations are being examined. India now has strong indigenous manufacturing capabilities and advanced technologies are already available within the current pricing framework. Any future price cap revision decision should be based on objective assessment of market data, patient affordability and the need to strengthen domestic manufacturing under the Make in India and Atmanirbhar Bharat initiatives.\"                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Online Bureau</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Online Bureau</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675629/ETHealthWorld\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ETHealthWorld</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Nov 17, 2026 at 02:52 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Nov 17, 2026 at 02:52 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n                      \n    \n            <p>\n                </p><h2>Join the community of 2M+ industry professionals. </h2>   \n                <h3>Subscribe to Newsletter to get latest insights &amp; analysis in your inbox.</h3>\n            <p></p>\n\n           